(doc
  (title "YX — Build Status")
  (source-format markdown)
  (converted "2026-07-19")
  (para "**Author:** Scott D. Yelich · **Updated:** 2026-07-19 · **Version:** 2.1.0")
  (section
    (heading "Done")
    (item "**Production implementation re-homed from sdts** — the v2.0.0 code that runs AlgoTrader's service mesh is now the canonical source of truth in this repo; sdts consumes yx back as a git-submodule dependency (AlgoTrader mesh + ib-bridge trading adapter).")
    (item "**Swift + Python wire parity** — byte-identical wire format (`HMAC-SHA256(16B) + GUID(6B) + payload`; Protocol 0 text/JSON-RPC, Protocol 1 v2.0 binary with 65,535 channels, chunking, per-channel sequences; optional AES-256-GCM). Swift is the base (ADR D09, SPM); Python is wire-parity validation + the Python-bound edges (ib_async, MLX). No pip distribution.")
    (item "**Live cross-language interop proven** (2026-07-19) — real Python↔Swift UDP messaging: two-node mutual discovery + cross-language message delivery (Swift node ↔ Python node), keyed from the Keychain. Two Swift transport bugs fixed to get there (fire-and-forget CLI keep-alive Task; actor-isolated blocking `recvfrom` starving the receive loop).")
    (item "**`yxkey` + Keychain key management** (ADR D08) — mesh HMAC keys in the macOS Keychain (service `org.spy.yx`); `generate|set|get|list|remove`, `set` reads stdin; resolution `--key` > `YX_KEY` > Keychain > dev key (loud warning). Python mirror in `src/python/yx_key.py`. Spec: `protocol/specs/architecture/key-management.sxp`.")
    (item "**`yxnode` mesh node daemon** — presence heartbeat (`node.hello`), `node.info` RPC, and `msg.deliver` → Unified Node Format (UNF) markdown to `~/ai/mail/YYYY/MM/<id>.md` for locally-addressed agents. Swift = production, Python = spec-proof."))
  (section
    (heading "Tests")
    (table
      (row "Suite" "Count" "Status")
      (row "Swift (`swift test`)" "94" "passing")
      (row "Python (`pytest`, `src/python/tests/`)" "47" "passing"))
    (para "Interop: proven via live cross-language node tests + the unit suites. The older line's formal 52-test interop matrix has **not** been re-run against v2 framing (`tests/interop-v1-legacy/`). The sdts consumer suite (`tests/yx-interop/`) does run 28/28 against v2, including 0x03 MULTI-CHUNK with asserted packet counts (added 2026-08-02) — on macOS only; a Linux build of Swift YX is UNVERIFIED and currently impossible without porting CryptoKit/Compression/Darwin sockets."))
  (section
    (heading "Next / not done")
    (item "**Message-bus reliability layer** — ack/retry/dedup on top of best-effort UDP.")
    (item "**Re-run the formal 52-test interop matrix** adapted to v2 framing (now 13 scenarios/combination — scenario 5 is 0x03 MULTI-CHUNK).")
    (item "**Bonjour/mDNS discovery** (ADR D10) — designed-for; broadcast only today.")
    (item "**`msg` client CLI** — send messages into the mesh without running a node.")
    (item "**laniakea launchd deploy** — stand yxnode up as a supervised service (laniakea `svc`).")
    (item "Mesh-key distribution is manual (per-node Keychain) — no automated rollout.")
    (para "See `README.md` (layout + quick start), `docs/yx.sxp` (executive summary), and `protocol/specs/architecture/ybs-decisions.sxp` (ADRs D08/D09/D10).")))
